<title>BELGIUM: BELGIAN AWARD FOR PINAULT-PRINTEMPS BOSS.</title>
<headline>BELGIAN AWARD FOR PINAULT-PRINTEMPS BOSS.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgium is to award Francois Pinault, chairman of French retail group Pinault-Printemps-La Redoute SA, a prize in recognition of his role in fostering closer economic ties between France and Belgium, the Royal Palace announced on Friday.</p>
<p>Pinault is to receive the 1996 &quot;Mercurius Belge&quot; prize at a ceremony with Belgium's Prince Philippe on March 20.</p>
<p>The award comes against the background of strained economic ties between France and Belgium following news from French carmaker Renault at the end of February that it would close its Belgian plant, sparking a wave of industrial unrest.</p>
<p>A Palace spokeswoman could not immediately confirm when it was decided to make the award to Pinault.</p>
<p>-- Nick Antonovics, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6817, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
